-- title:
--   Sections of the resolved model avoid the edge points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ together with a ring homomorphism $O \to \kappa$, and let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a `DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O κ toκ`, so in particular a scheme $Y$ with a proper flat structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ that is regular and of stalk Krull dimension at most $2$ along the fibre over $p$, carrying a finite set of nodes $n$ with widths $\mathrm{width}(n) \ge 1$ and an invertible ideal sheaf $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}(c)$ for each $c$ in $X0MqComponents\ \mathrm{width} = \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_n \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n)-1)$. Let $\sigma$ be a section of the structure morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} O$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ whose composite with $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$ is the identity. Then the image $y$ of the closed point of $O$ under the underlying map of $\sigma$ satisfies: $y \ne \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{edgePt}\,n\,d$ for every node $n$ and every $d : \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n))$; $y$ lies in $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$; and there is exactly one index $c$ with $y$ in the support of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}(c)$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a section of a regular model over a discrete valuation ring meets the special fibre in a smooth point, hence lies on a single irreducible component and avoids the intersection points of components; here it is specialised to the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of the modular curve and its distinguished edge points. It is used in the construction of sections with prescribed behaviour on the relative Picard functor, via [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective).
